WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.587
It likes to describe itself as

00:00:04.587 --> 00:00:07.424
 the biggest car brand you've never heard of.

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:13.638
Now, China's BYD has overtaken Tesla

00:00:13.638 --> 00:00:16.933
as the world's
largest seller of electric vehicles.

00:00:18.643 --> 00:00:21.104
Even if you've never heard of BYD,

00:00:21.104 --> 00:00:23.481
there's a chance
you've been in one of its busses.

00:00:28.445 --> 00:00:29.779
While its taxis prowl

00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:32.532
the streets of some of the world's
biggest cities.

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:36.578
But busses and taxis 

00:00:36.578 --> 00:00:39.789
aren’t the reason why BYD has overtaken Tesla.

00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:43.168
Instead, it's the fruit of long-term
strategic thinking

00:00:43.168 --> 00:00:46.254
on the part of BYD itself
and the Chinese government.

00:00:47.422 --> 00:00:48.465
And it’s setting China up

00:00:48.465 --> 00:00:52.719
to be the dominant global player
in the transportation of the future:

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:54.220
electric vehicles,

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:58.141
a business that could be worth 
$8.8 trillion by the end of the decade.

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:04.439
Here are the three most important things
that have made BYD the king of EVs.

00:01:10.195 --> 00:01:11.404
The Chinese government

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:14.199
has played a huge role in BYD's rise.

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:20.163
We've arguably never seen anything like
this in terms of the amount of support

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:23.708
that China has extended to automakers,

00:01:23.792 --> 00:01:26.795
specifically pertaining to EVs.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:31.925
Beijing has given an estimated $30 billion
of tax exemptions to the industry

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:36.721
since 2010, and may wave a further 
$97 billion by 2027.

00:01:37.722 --> 00:01:41.142
China actually takes a carrot
and stick approach.

00:01:41.559 --> 00:01:44.229
They set mandatory EV

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:48.525
output targets for automakers,
but they also offer cheaper

00:01:48.525 --> 00:01:53.363
loans and cheaper land
and R&amp;D subsidies to all those EV makers.

00:01:53.905 --> 00:01:56.574
And BYD has been a massive beneficiary of that.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:00.286
It's still sells most of its
electric vehicles in its home market.

00:02:00.912 --> 00:02:04.791
But of course, Tesla has also benefited
from Chinese subsidies,

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:08.545
which is where the second reason
for BYD’s rise comes in.

00:02:13.925 --> 00:02:17.971
Most of BYD's cars are simply a lot
cheaper than Tesla's.

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:21.015
In fact, it sells ten popular models, 

00:02:21.015 --> 00:02:23.810
starting from less than Tesla's cheapest offering 

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.311
for the Model 3 sedan.

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:29.357
And BYD sells a lot more
of the cheaper vehicles in its lineup.

00:02:30.024 --> 00:02:34.571
They have very cheap models
starting from $10,000.

00:02:34.571 --> 00:02:37.907
Their approach has been 
extremely different in the sense that

00:02:37.907 --> 00:02:40.785
Elon Musk believed that
you had to sort of start from the high end

00:02:40.785 --> 00:02:45.331
with a sexy performance car
to get people interested in electric cars

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:47.417
and then work your 
way down the price spectrum.

00:02:47.792 --> 00:02:53.381
BYD went at it from the other end
where it was about cheap taxis and busses

00:02:53.381 --> 00:02:57.302
that needed a heck of a lot of batteries
and really sort of, you know, drove down

00:02:57.302 --> 00:03:01.222
the prices of the batteries
that they could put into passenger cars.

00:03:02.098 --> 00:03:05.560
While the average price paid 
for a Tesla is about $45,000,

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:08.479
the average BYD sells
for roughly half that.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:13.151
That, of course, raises the question,
how can it sell them so cheaply?

00:03:14.611 --> 00:03:16.362
The secret to that price tag

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:19.365
lies in what is known as vertical integration.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.785
Our vertical integration capability

00:03:22.785 --> 00:03:28.499
give us the flexibility,
the faster response to the market trend

00:03:29.125 --> 00:03:31.002
as well as the better spot

00:03:31.002 --> 00:03:33.796
for brand developing and customer service.

00:03:34.464 --> 00:03:36.925
That's a fancy way of saying 
that they make a lot

00:03:36.925 --> 00:03:39.928
of the things that go into 
their vehicles themselves.

00:03:40.303 --> 00:03:43.348
Carmakers usually buy most 
components from suppliers

00:03:43.348 --> 00:03:46.309
such as Bosch, Continental and Aptiv.

00:03:47.352 --> 00:03:53.441
Volkswagen, for instance, only makes
35% of the parts in its ID.3 electric car.

00:03:53.441 --> 00:03:56.152
Tesla, meanwhile, makes 68% of the parts

00:03:56.152 --> 00:04:00.031
that go into its Model 3 made in the US.

00:04:00.031 --> 00:04:05.286
BYD makes 75% of the parts
that go into the Seal, its flagship model.

00:04:05.787 --> 00:04:08.790
The most important factor is that BYD

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:13.169
is the only automaker that 
produces all of its batteries in-house.

00:04:13.628 --> 00:04:17.840
That was hugely important
during the pandemic when the supply chains

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:21.761
were just absolutely in a 
state of chaos for the industry.

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:26.849
The fact that BYD was in control
of its own destiny gave them a huge leg up

00:04:26.849 --> 00:04:31.187
over the rest of the industry, and
especially as it pertains to batteries.

00:04:31.187 --> 00:04:34.148
This is a company
that has been in the battery space

00:04:34.148 --> 00:04:36.150
since the 1990s. 

00:04:37.694 --> 00:04:40.697
BYD actually stands for Build Your Dreams.

00:04:40.697 --> 00:04:44.826
It started out in 1995
as a battery company.

00:04:44.826 --> 00:04:48.204
They make rechargeable batteries
for mobile phones and other

00:04:48.204 --> 00:04:49.706
electronics products.

00:04:49.706 --> 00:04:54.127
And then the company
got into the auto business in 2003.

00:04:54.711 --> 00:04:59.757
Making its own batteries and other
components helps it reduce a lot of costs.

00:04:59.757 --> 00:05:02.135
That's attracted some big name investors.

00:05:02.677 --> 00:05:05.555
Call it the continued BYD
promotional roadshow.

00:05:05.555 --> 00:05:07.181
And investor Warren Buffett 

00:05:07.181 --> 00:05:10.476
brought his buddy Bill Gates
along for the ride here in Beijing.

00:05:10.727 --> 00:05:11.769
It was fantastic.

00:05:11.769 --> 00:05:14.355
I’m amazed at the quality of that vehicle.

00:05:14.355 --> 00:05:17.025
Warren Buffett was one of 
the biggest early investors

00:05:17.025 --> 00:05:20.236
in BYD through his holding company,
Berkshire Hathaway.

00:05:21.112 --> 00:05:23.740
And the battery technology
might also give BYD

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:26.743
a technological edge over some rivals.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:30.830
It uses lithium-iron-phosphate,
which is not only cheaper

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:34.542
than other batteries,
it's also packaged a lot more compactly.

00:05:35.543 --> 00:05:40.715
And chemistry is a core expertise
of founder Wang Chuanfu.

00:05:40.715 --> 00:05:42.508
He’s sort of the anti-Elon Musk.

00:05:43.134 --> 00:05:47.472
Wang is a chemist by training
and an engineer.

00:05:47.472 --> 00:05:49.599
And an anecdote
that one of our reporters was told

00:05:49.599 --> 00:05:52.310
was that when he was told
he needed to dress up a bit

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:56.773
for an investor meeting, he stopped to buy
shirts just sort of off the street.

00:05:56.773 --> 00:06:02.153
And so he's far from one of the flashier
executives in the auto industry.

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:20.254
This has all set BYD up to be
the biggest player in electric vehicles.

00:06:21.506 --> 00:06:22.965
The question now is whether

00:06:22.965 --> 00:06:26.094
it can become one of the world's
biggest carmakers full stop.

00:06:27.178 --> 00:06:30.014
And that means growing outside of China.

00:06:30.556 --> 00:06:32.725
In 2021, BYD started to 

00:06:32.725 --> 00:06:35.269
step up its global expansion.

00:06:35.269 --> 00:06:36.312
It started to launch more 

00:06:36.312 --> 00:06:38.981
passenger vehicles across the global markets,

00:06:38.981 --> 00:06:42.151
including Middle East, Southeast Asia 

00:06:42.151 --> 00:06:43.319
and Europe.

00:06:43.319 --> 00:06:46.239
It's still a very new entrant
in global markets.

00:06:46.239 --> 00:06:49.075
The volume contribution
is rising, but still small.

00:06:50.159 --> 00:06:51.119
Even so,

00:06:51.119 --> 00:06:53.830
BYD inside three years
has become one of the top-selling

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:58.668
EV brands in markets
such as Thailand, Brazil and Australia.

00:06:59.669 --> 00:07:03.840
It also remains to be seen
whether this company can quickly

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:06.467
grow in some of these newer markets

00:07:06.467 --> 00:07:09.846
that it's entering where it isn't
well-known, it isn't recognized.

00:07:10.972 --> 00:07:15.560
The two most prominent challenges in 
BYD’s global expansion will be

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:20.189
first regulatory uncertainties
and second brand awareness.

00:07:20.189 --> 00:07:25.069
The European Union is investigating
into Chinese EV subsidies.

00:07:25.486 --> 00:07:30.408
Chinese automakers, they are exporting
more of their EVs into Europe.

00:07:30.408 --> 00:07:35.913
Because those cars are produced in China
so the production costs are pretty low,

00:07:35.913 --> 00:07:38.833
which allows the automakers
to set their prices

00:07:38.833 --> 00:07:43.004
in Europe cheaper than the 
European counterparts, which 

00:07:43.004 --> 00:07:46.048
has been very alarming
to the European auto industry.

00:07:46.466 --> 00:07:50.094
One way around that will be to increase
the amount of local production.

00:07:50.761 --> 00:07:53.598
Definitely, localization is one of the very

00:07:53.598 --> 00:07:57.268
important strategy of BYD’s Europe strategy.

00:07:57.268 --> 00:07:59.812
And so we are considering, we are evaluating 

00:07:59.812 --> 00:08:02.106
different locations in Europe

00:08:02.106 --> 00:08:03.649
and where we can build the cars.

00:08:04.442 --> 00:08:08.237
And apart from busses
and trucks, BYD isn’t in the US.

00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:12.366
The trade tensions
between Beijing and Washington

00:08:12.366 --> 00:08:16.871
are keeping BYD back and giving them pause
to entering the US market.

00:08:17.538 --> 00:08:21.876
For years, automotive experts
have predicted established carmaking giants

00:08:21.876 --> 00:08:22.835
like GM, 

00:08:22.835 --> 00:08:23.878
Volkswagen

00:08:23.878 --> 00:08:25.046
or Toyota

00:08:25.046 --> 00:08:27.632
would catch up with Tesla
in electric vehicles.

00:08:28.508 --> 00:08:29.509
In hindsight,

00:08:29.509 --> 00:08:33.387
it probably shouldn't be a surprise
that a Chinese rival got there first.

